RIM Conditional Statements Example
RIM Demonstrates IZ command for conditionals

ECKO Testing conditional statements...
ECKO

RIM Test equality
SEP value1 = hello
SEP value2 = hello
IZ %value1% == %value2% ECKO value1 equals value2

SEP value3 = world
IZ %value1% == %value3% ECKO This should not print

RIM Test inequality
IZ %value1% != %value3% ECKO value1 does not equal value3

RIM Conditional with string literals
SEP status = active
IZ %status% == active ECKO Status is active
IZ %status% == inactive ECKO Status is inactive

RIM Test with numbers
SEP count = 5
IZ %count% == 5 ECKO Count is five
IZ %count% != 10 ECKO Count is not ten

ECKO
ECKO All conditional tests complete!
